{ First of all, look at these 6 Building Blocks positions. Once done, continue the Flowchart understanding.

A dead draw

This is a position you already have in your internal “basics” database. As long as white’s King stays on h2 or g2, and as long as the Rook remains on the a-file and checks the black King every time it touches its pawn, the game can’t be won. }
1... Kf5 (1... Kf6 2. Kf2 (2. Kf3 Rf1+ { [%cal Ga2a1] }) (2. Kg3 Rg1+) 2... Rh1 { [%csl Gh1,Ga2][%cal Gh1h2,Gh2a2] } 3. Rxa2 (3. Kg2 a1=Q 4. Rxa1 Rxa1 { [%csl Ga1] }) 3... Rh2+ { [%csl Ga2][%cal Gh2a2] }) 2. Kh2 (2. Ra5+ Ke4 3. Ra4+ Kd3 4. Ra3+ (4. Ra7 Kc2 5. Rc7+ Kb3 6. Rb7+ Kc4 7. Rc7+ Kb5 8. Ra7 Kb6 9. Ra8 Kb7 { [%csl Ga3] } 10. Ra3 Kb6 11. Ra8 Kb7 12. Ra3) 4... Kc2 5. Ra8 Kb2 6. Rb8+ Kc3 7. Rc8+ Kb4 8. Rb8+ Ka5 9. Ra8+ Kb6 10. Ra3 (10. Rb8+ Ka7 11. Rb2 Rg1+ 12. Kxg1 a1=Q+ { [%csl Gb2][%cal Ga1b2] }) 10... Kb5 11. Kh2 (11. Ra8 Kb6 12. Ra3 Kc5 13. Ra5+ Kb4 14. Ra8 Kb3 15. Rb8+) 11... Kb4 12. Ra8 Kb5 13. Rb8+ Ka6 14. Ra8+ Kb7 15. Ra3) (2. Kg3 Rg1+ { [%csl Gg3,Ga1][%cal Gg1g3,Ga2a1] }) (2. Kf2 Rh1 3. Rxa2 { [%csl Gh2,Ga2][%cal Gh1h2,Gh2a2] } (3. Ke3 a1=Q) (3. Ke2 a1=Q 4. Rxa1 Rxa1) 3... Rh2+ { [%csl Ga2][%cal Gh2a2] }) (2. Rb7 Rg1+ 3. Kxg1 a1=Q+ { [%csl Gg1][%cal Ga1g1] }) (2. Kf3 Rf1+ { [%csl Ga1,Gf4][%cal Ga2a1,Gf1f4] } 3. Ke2 (3. Ke3 a1=Q 4. Rxa1 Rxa1 { [%csl Ga1] }) 3... a1=Q 4. Rxa1 Rxa1 { [%csl Ga1] }) 2... Ke4 3. Kg2 Kd3 4. Kh2 Kc2 5. Rc7+ (5. Kg2 Kb2 6. Rb7+ Ka3 7. Ra7+ Kb4 8. Rb7+ Ka5 9. Ra7+ Kb6 10. Ra3 Kb5 11. Ra8 Kb6 12. Ra3 Kb5 13. Ra8 Kb4 14. Rb8+ Kc5 15. Rd8 (15. Rc8+ Kb6 { [%csl Gb8][%cal Gc8b8] } 16. Rb8+ (16. Ra8) 16... Ka7 { [%cal Ga8a1] })) 5... Kb2 6. Rb7+ Kc2 7. Rc7+ Kb3 8. Rb7+ Kc4 9. Ra7 (9. Rc7+ Kb5 10. Ra7 Kb6) 9... Kb5 { [%csl Ga2][%cal Ga7a2] } 10. Rb7+ { [%cal Gb7b1,Gb5a6] } (10. Ra8 Kb4 (10... Kb6 11. Ra3) 11. Rb8+ Ka5 12. Ra8+ Kb6 13. Rb8+ Ka7) (10. Ra3 Kb4 11. Ra8 { [%csl Ga2][%cal Ga8a2] } 11... Kb3 12. Rb8+ Kc2 13. Rc8+) 10... Ka6 11. Rb2 { [%csl Gh1][%cal Ga1h1] } (11. Rb8 Ka7 12. Rb2 Rh1+ { [%csl Gh2][%cal Gh1h2] } 13. Kxh1 a1=Q+ { [%csl Gb2][%cal Ga1b2] }) 11... Rh1+ 12. Kxh1 a1=Q+ { [%csl Gb2][%cal Ga1b2] } *


