{ White should resign

RULE
King and Rooklose vs. King, Rook, a-pawn on the 7th (with its Rook trapped in front of it), and an f-pawn.

New and very important! The win is suddenly effortless since the f-pawn will successfully pull white’s King off of both critical squares on h2 and g2. Infact, Black doesn’t even need to use his King to claim to full point. }
1... f4 { [%cal Gf4f3,Gf3f2] } (1... Kg5) 2. Ra8 (2. Ra6+ { doesn’t accomplish anything since black’s King would just march towards the Rook } 2... Kf7 (2... Kf5 3. Ra5+ Ke6 4. Ra6+ Kd5 5. Ra5+ Kc6 6. Ra6+ Kb5 7. Ra8 f3+ 8. Kh2 f2 9. Rf8 f1=Q 10. Rxf1 Rxf1 11. Kg2 Rf7 (11... a1=Q 12. Kg3 Qg7+ 13. Kh3 Rh1#) 12. Kg3) (2... Kg5 3. Ra5+ Kg4 4. Ra4 Kg5 5. Ra5+ Kf6 6. Ra4 Ke5 7. Ra3 Kd4 8. Ra4+ Kc3 9. Ra3+ Kb4 10. Ra8 f3+ 11. Kxf3 (11. Kh2 f2 12. Rf8 Rh1+ 13. Kxh1 a1=Q+) 11... Rf1+) 3. Ra7+ Ke6 4. Ra6+ Kd7 5. Ra7+ Kc6 6. Ra6+ Kb7 { and then continue pushing the f-pawn once the checks ended. }) 2... f3+! 3. Kh2 { [%csl Rh2][%cal Gf3f2] } (3. Kxf3 { [%csl Gf1][%cal Ga1f1] } 3... Rf1+ { [%csl Ga1][%cal Ga2a1] } 4. Kg2 a1=Q $19) (3. Kf2 Rh1 { [%csl Ra2] } 4. Rxa2 Rh2+ $19 { [%cal Gh2a2] }) 3... f2 $19 { [%csl Gf1] } 4. Rf8 { [%csl Ga2][%cal Gf2f1] } 4... Rh1+ { [%csl Gh1,Ga1][%cal Ga2a1] } 5. Kxh1 a1=Q+ 6. Kg2 Qg1+ *


