{ White wins

This “shuffle defense” isn’t possible if the pawn is a bishop-pawn—then the side diagonal is shortened and zugzwangs appear. } { [%csl Bf8][%cal Rc3g7,Gg7f8] }
1. Bg7 Bb4 2. Bf8 { [%csl Rf8] } 2... Bd2 3. Bc5 (3. Be7 Bh6 { [%csl Gh6] } 4. Bf8 Bd2) 3... Bh6 { Our first goal has been reached, and black’s Bishop is now stuck on the uncomfortably short h6-f8 diagonal. Next stop, zugzwang! } 4. Bd4! { Suddenly Black has no good move! } { [%csl Bf8][%cal Rd4g7,Bf7f8] } 4... Kf5 (4... Kg5 5. Be3+ $18) 5. Bg7 $18 { [%csl Rf8][%cal Rf7f8] } *


