{ Black to move
Is Black doomed? }
1... Rd1 { Creating maximum Checking Distance!
It’s too late to set up a Philidor Position, but he can still save himself by using our “Philidor gone bad” formula:
- Activate the Rook
- Place it behind the pawn
- Run the King to the Short Side of the board.
- Make sure you create Checking Distance for your Rook. } { [%cal Ga5b6] } (1... Rd7?? 2. Rxd7 Kxd7 3. Kb6 Kc8 4. Kc6 $18) 2. Kb6 Rc1!! (2... Rb1+? 3. Kc6 Kb8 4. Rh8+ Ka7 5. Kc7 Rg1 6. Rh7 Rg8 7. c6 (7. Kc6+ Kb8) 7... Rf8 8. Kd6+ Kb8 9. c7+ (9. Kd7 Rc8 10. Kd6 Rf8 (10... Rg8 11. Rb7+ Kc8 12. Ra7 Rg6+ 13. Ke7 { [%cal Gg6g7] } (13. Kc5 Kb8 14. Rb7+ Kc8 15. Kb6 Rg1))) 9... Kc8 10. Kc6 Rf6+ 11. Kc5 Ra6) 3. Kc6 (3. Rh8+ Kd7 { White can’t make any progress Kd7since black’s Rook and King make c6 impossible. }) 3... Kb8! { Goingto the Short Side of the board so the Rook can have Checking Distance on the kingside. } 4. Rh8+ Ka7 5. Rc8 (5. Kd6 Kb7! $10) 5... Rh1! { Creating optimum Checking Distance and threatening to slide back into a perfect Philidor with 6...Rh6+. } 6. Rd8 Rc1! $10 { White can’t make any progress. } (6... Rh6+ 7. Kc7 Rh7+ 8. Rd7) *


