1. Bb7 { White would not win an analogous position with a center pawn (with the Kings facing off), but here the shortened second diagonal (a6-c8) allows White
to claim victory: } 1... Bg4 2. Bc8 Be2 3. Bf5 Ba6 4. Be4! $18 { and Black must resign since any King move allows Bb7, while a Bishop move either hangs the Bishop or allows White to make a Queen. } *


