{ White to move
Should White keep the Rooks on or exchange by Rxf6? }
1. Rxf6! { White feared the King and pawn endgame that would occur after 1.Rxf6, so he tried 1.Rd2 and went on to lose.
However, taking on f6 by 1.Rxf6 would have given White an outside passed pawn, and this would have allowed him to save the game } (1. Rd2? a5 2. Kg4 Kh7 3. h5 b5 4. Kg5 Re6 5. Kf5 Re1 6. Rc2 Rh1 7. Kg4 Rb1 8. Kf4 a4 9. Kf5 c5 10. Ke4 Kh6 11. Kf5 b4 12. axb4 cxb4 13. Rg2 a3 14. bxa3 bxa3 15. Ra2 Rb3 16. Kg4 Rb4+ 17. Kf5 Rb5+ 18. Kf4 Ra5 19. Kg4 Ra4+ 20. Kf5 Kxh5 21. Rh2+ Rh4 22. Rg2 g6+ 23. Kf6 Rf4+ $19 { NN- Staunton, London 1842 }) 1... gxf6 2. Kg4 Kf7 3. h5 c5 4. Kf5 b5 5. h6 c4 (5... a5 6. h7 Kg7 7. h8=Q+ Kxh8 8. Kxf6 b4 9. axb4 cxb4 10. Ke5 a4 11. Kd4 $10) 6. h7 Kg7 7. h8=Q+ Kxh8 8. Kxf6 a5 9. Ke5 b4 10. axb4 axb4 11. Kd4 $10 *


