{ White to move
Is 1.Rc8 a good move? }
1. Rc8 { Placing a Rook behind a passed pawnis often important, and that rule holds true here since Black threatened to win with ...c2. By stopping the pawn with 1.Rc8, white’s material advantage will ultimately prevail. } 1... Ka4 (1... Rc4 2. Rxc4 Kxc4 3. Ke2 $18 { easy for white }) 2. h5 Re6 3. f3 a5 4. g4 fxg4 5. fxg4 Rh6 (5... Re4 6. h6 Rxg4 7. h7 Rh4 8. h8=Q Rxh8 9. Rxh8 Ka3 10. Ke2 $18) 6. Ke2 Ka3 7. Rxc3+ Kxa2 8. Rc5 a4 9. Rb5 a3 10. Kf3 Ka1 11. Ra5 (11. Kf4 a2 12. Kg5 Rxh5+ 13. Kxh5 $10 { stalemate }) 11... a2 12. Kg3 Kb2 13. Kh4 a1=Q 14. Rxa1 Kxa1 15. g5 Ra6 16. h6 Ra7 17. g6 Ra4+ 18. Kg5 Ra5+ 19. Kf4 Ra4+ 20. Ke5 Ra5+ 21. Kd4 Ra4+ 22. Kc5 { 1-0. Szen - Newham, London 1851.
An impressive performance by the legendary Szen. Hardto believe they were playing such fine endgames way back in 1851! } *


